<title>SWITZERLAND: Ascom selling Nexion unit to Fujitsu unit.</title>
<headline>Ascom selling Nexion unit to Fujitsu unit.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss telecommunications group Ascom said it will sell its U.S. development company Ascom Nexion to a U.S. subsidiary of Fujitsu Ltd for a gross sum of $130 million.</p>
<p>The amount is less transaction costs.</p>
<p>The sale, subject to approval of U.S. authorities, involves Fujitsu's U.S. subsidiary, Fujitsu Network Communications.</p>
<p>&quot;Ascom announced the pending sale at this year's annual results press conference on April 16, but it was agreed at the time by both parties to await disclosure of the purchaser's name and the transaction price,&quot; Ascom said in a brief statement.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
